  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate the variable $h.$ To do this, we treat $k$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nIn this case, we simply multiply both sides of the equation by $8:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{h}{8} & =k \\\\ 8\\cdot \\frac{h}{8} & =8\\cdot k \\\\ \\cancel{8}\\cdot \\frac{h}{\\cancel{8}} & =8k \\\\ h & =8k\\end{aligned}\n$$",
